      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's possible that your partner may be entering a diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA) state, which is a potentially life-threatening complication of high blood sugar. In this case, giving them more water and letting them sleep may not be the best course of action, as high blood sugar levels can be accompanied by nausea, vomiting, and dizziness. Instead, you should try to get them to drink 7-10 non-carb drinks (like water or clear broth) to hopefully raise their urine output and help clear excess glucose from their system.",
